<node>
    <node name="description" channel="inline" format="text/plain" model="Loops the programme flow from the given start to the given end in the given steps.

The comparison of index and end value is exclusive, that is it does not
consider the end value in the executed model since the loop is left before:
- positive step: if (index &#x0026;#x003E;= endvalue) then break
- negative step: if (index &#x0026;#x003C;= endvalue) then break

If the property &#x0022;step&#x0022; contains a negative value, then the loop is running downwards.

Java example:

for (int i = 0; i &#x0026;#x003C; 10; i += 2) {
System.out.println(&#x0022;Hello&#x0022;);
}"/>
    <node name="examples" channel="file" format="text/plain" model="api-generator/spec/logic/flow/loop-for/examples.txt"/>
    <node name="properties" channel="file" format="element/part" model="api-generator/spec/logic/flow/loop-for/properties.cybol"/>
</node>
